ing's syndrome: unlikely without classic truncal obesity or skin changes"], "alarm_features": ["Unintentional weight loss (17 lbs in 1 month)", "Chronic heavy smoking (2 packs/day since age 25)", "Alcohol use (2-7 drinks/day)", "Hypertension (177/108 mmHg)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Neurological Disorders with Motor-Sensory Deficits", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.3225806451612904, "posterior": 0.2225890811041986, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Sensory loss suggests neural vs. musculoskeletal origin, weakly disfavoring musculoskeletal mimicry."], "evidence_against": ["Subacute progression is atypical for sudden vascular events, moderately weakening vascular explanations."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Thoracic Neoplasms with Paraneoplastic or Direct Involvement", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.31451612903225806, "posterior": 0.24444858260217794, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The subacute progression and focal weakness suggest possible mononeuropathy, providing weak clinical support for neurological disorders."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of chest symptoms weakly contradicts apical lung tumor's typical presentation."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3", "B2.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Vascular Disorders with Upper-Limb Ischemia", "level